*******************************************************************

    ISVGA256.BGI  --   A Super VGA BGI driver for Turbo C and Pascal
                       that integrates support for multiple SVGA chipsets
                       into one driver.

   ---------------------------------------
   | To order send:  $35.00 to:          |
   |             Thomas Design           |
   |             P.O. Box 586            |
   |             Stillwater Oklahoma     |
   |             74076                   |
   |                                     |
   | (Please use order form in this doc) |
   ---------------------------------------

                  --   Due to a limitation in both TC and TP you can't
                       use setgraphmode() to set a mode higher than 0ah
                       without patching the compilers.  A patch is supplied
                       in this archive that, using Borland's PATCH.COM,
                       will increase this limit to 40 modes.
                       To install the patch just run the PATGRPTC.BAT file.
                       Make sure Patch.com is in your search path.

                  --   Trident and Chips and Tech vga support is in the
                       driver.  Autodetect currently will not detect those
                       chipsets.  To use a vga card based on either of the
                       above two chipsets you need to force the BGI to use
                       ISVGA256.BGI and then use setgraphmode(...) to select
                       the appropriate mode.  Let us know what vga cards work
                       using those two chipsets.....


    Cards supported:  Video 7,  Paradise,  ATI,  Tecmar,  Orchid,  Genoa,
                      Compaq VGA, HP VGA, STB, Trident, and Chips 'n Tech
             Others:  If your VGA card uses the SVGA chipset from either:
                      Paradise or Tseng Labs your card will probably work
                      with these drivers.  The same should hold true for
                      the Trident and Chips 'n Tech chipset vga's.  You
                      may need to override autodetect.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Cost:  (registered owners of other $15 drivers pay: $25.00)
        (registered owners of 4 or more $15.00 drivers can upgrade free)
        (new buyers:             $35.00)


 Note:  the following are known bugs in the shareware versions of our drivers
        and have been fixed in the registered versions.
          --  Textwidth and Textheight returned the wrong values.
          --  Putimage/Getimage at certain x,y locations would fail

 Note:  All of the drivers have had another pass of optimizations done.
        Performance improvements are especially impressive in the 16-color
        drivers.
          --  Horizontal & Vertical vectors now use their own high speed
              routines.
          --  16-color mode solid fills use their own high speed routine.
          --  Bank-selection in extended VGA modes doesn't impact the
              graphics routines nearly as much due to JUMP optimization.

